        {% endif %}
    </tbody>
</table>
<p style="font-size: 7pt; color: #718096;">Raw component scores are normalized against their measured S&amp;P 500 distributions before weighting, so each weight carries its stated influence. Where narrative sections quote a raw analyst score (e.g. the value factor), the axis shown here is that reading after normalization — the two can differ slightly by design. Quality and valuation are kept as separate axes — the rating is read from the pair, and price alone never produces a Sell.</p>
{% else %}
<table class="data-table">
    <thead>
        <tr><th>Component</th><th style="text-align: right;">Score</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {% if stock.moat_breakdown.financial_health is not none %}<tr><td>Financial Health</td><td class="num">{{ "%.1f"|format(stock.moat_breakdown.financial_health) }}/10</td></tr>{% endif %}
